  "issuedISO": "2026-11-25T15:45:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "An extra-large north-northwest (330 to 350 degree) swell will build quickly this evening and tonight, peaking well above warning levels early Thursday. This will bring extra-large to giant warning-level surf to north and west-facing shores, possibly lingering into Friday. Therefore, a High Surf Warning is in effect for north and west-facing shores of Niihau, Kauai, Oahu, Molokai, and north facing shores of Maui and the Big Island. A High Surf Advisory is in effect for west facing shores of Maui. The swell will gradually fade through the weekend. Surf heights along east-facing shores will be somewhat elevated through Friday due to wrapping from the north-northwest swell, but are expected to remain below advisory levels. Surf along south-facing shores will remain tiny to small through the next few days.",
